From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:22:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm: google: gs-decon: hold the boot framebuffer's aperture

gs-decon evicts simpledrm from the boot framebuffer, but on raven
simpledrm probed 30 ms after gs-decon registered, found the aperture
free and stayed: Hyprland drove it as a second, invisible monitor
(Unknown-1) next to the panel. After the eviction, acquire the range
too, so a later simpledrm fails its own acquire with -EBUSY.

Only gs101 holds it: it adds a failure path to probe, and the Pixel 7
Pro (gs201) has not shown the race.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/google/gs-decon.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/google/gs-decon.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/google/gs-decon.c
index 6f1c8c8a0..68875de48 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/google/gs-decon.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/google/gs-decon.c
@@ -269,6 +269,8 @@ struct gs_decon_soc_data {
 	bool start_hw_trigger;
 	/* the bootloader leaves MIF and DISP above the 120 Hz floors */
 	bool floors_optional;
+	/* hold the boot framebuffer's aperture after evicting simpledrm */
+	bool hold_boot_fb;
 };
 
 static const struct gs_decon_soc_data gs201_decon_data = {
@@ -289,6 +291,7 @@ static const struct gs_decon_soc_data gs101_decon_data = {
 	.image_size_reg = RDMA_IMG_SIZE,
 	.source_offset_reg = RDMA_SRC_OFFSET,
 	.shadow_update_mask = SHD_REG_UP_REQ_FLIP(SHD_REG_UP_REQ_ALL_WIN),
+	.hold_boot_fb = true,
 };
 
 static const struct gs_decon_soc_data zumapro_decon_data = {
@@ -1546,6 +1549,17 @@ static int gs_decon_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 						  gs_decon_driver.name);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_irqs;
+	/*
+	 * and keep it: on raven simpledrm probed 30 ms after us, found the
+	 * aperture free and stayed as a second, phantom output. Holding the
+	 * range makes its own acquire fail with -EBUSY.
+	 */
+	if (dc->soc->hold_boot_fb) {
+		ret = devm_aperture_acquire_for_platform_device(pdev, dc->boot_fb.start,
+								resource_size(&dc->boot_fb));
+		if (ret)
+			goto err_irqs;
+	}
 
 	dc->kms = true;
 	ret = drm_dev_register(&dc->drm, 0);
